    <bpmn:process id="W_W891" name="W891. Customer Bad Debt Write-Off Proposal &amp; Approval" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Account &gt; 180 days overdue with exhausted collection efforts; or customer bankruptcy/closure confirmed
Frequency: ~10–20 bad debt write-off events/year (per W81)
Volume: Average write-off: PHP 100,000–1,000,000; annual bad debt target: &lt; 0.5% of B2B revenue
Owner: Credit Manager / Finance Controller
Participants: Collection Agent, Credit Manager, Finance Controller, CFO, Legal Counsel, External Auditor
Source: workflow W891 — Customer Bad Debt Write-Off Proposal &amp; Approval</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W891_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W891_Lane1" name="Collection Agent">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W891_Lane2" name="Credit Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W891_Lane3" name="Legal Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W891_Lane4" name="Finance Controller">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W891_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W891_Start6" name="Account &gt; 180 days overdue with exhausted collection efforts; or customer…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task7" name="Identify write-off candidate — Collection Agent or Credit Manager identifies…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Identify write-off candidate — Collection Agent or Credit Manager identifies account meeting write-off criteria: (a) &gt; 180 days overdue, (b) 3+ collection calls with no response or broken promises, (c) no active orders in 90+ days, (d) customer confirmed closed/bankrupt, or (e) legal collection deemed cost-prohibitive
Responsible (R): Collection Agent
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task8" name="Compile write-off proposal — document: (a) account history (credit since date…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Compile write-off proposal — document: (a) account history (credit since date, total sales, payment pattern), (b) collection history (calls made, promises broken, last contact), (c) overdue invoice detail, (d) reason for write-off (bankruptcy, unresponsive, dispute, other), (e) legal opinion (if applicable), (f) recovery potential assessment (any assets or guarantors), (g) proposed write-off amount
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task9" name="Evaluate legal collection option — for amounts &gt; PHP 500,000: Legal Counsel…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Evaluate legal collection option — for amounts &gt; PHP 500,000: Legal Counsel assesses viability of legal action — cost of litigation vs. recovery probability; recommend legal action or write-off
Responsible (R): Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task10" name="Obtain write-off approval — authorization: (a) ≤ PHP 50,000: Finance Manager +…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Obtain write-off approval — authorization: (a) ≤ PHP 50,000: Finance Manager + Controller, (b) PHP 50,001–200,000: CFO, (c) PHP 200,001–1,000,000: CEO + CFO, (d) &gt; PHP 1,000,000: Board resolution (aligned to W81&#x27;s write-off authority ladder); each approver reviews proposal and supporting documentation
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO / CEO
Duration: 30 min per approval level</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task11" name="Execute write-off — (a) post bad debt expense in GL, (b) reverse AR balance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Execute write-off — (a) post bad debt expense in GL, (b) reverse AR balance, (c) update customer status to &quot;Written Off&quot;, (d) apply credit block to prevent future orders, (e) update allowance for doubtful accounts, (f) file BIR documentation for bad debt deduction (requires BIR-permitted evidence of collection efforts)
Responsible (R): Finance Controller
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task12" name="External collection agency referral (optional) — for write-offs &gt; PHP 200,000…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: External collection agency referral (optional) — for write-offs &gt; PHP 200,000 with identifiable customer: refer to external collection agency on contingency basis (typically 15–25% of recovered amount); track recovery
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 1 hour</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W891_Task13" name="Annual bad debt review — compile annual write-off summary: (a) total write-offs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Annual bad debt review — compile annual write-off summary: (a) total write-offs vs. target (&lt; 0.5% of B2B revenue), (b) root cause analysis, (c) industry and geographic concentration, (d) credit scoring model accuracy, (e) recommendations for portfolio improvement
Responsible (R): Credit Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W891_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W891_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W891_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W891_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-288 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Payment &amp; Settlement (PA-16.3).) | - operational: Credit Manager / Finance Controller review and approval gate
Owner: Credit Manager / Finance Controller</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W891_Assoc16" sourceRef="W891_Annotation15" targetRef="W891_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
