      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1326" name="W1326. Customer B2B Project Payment Plan Negotiation, Arrears Management &amp; Restructuring" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Corporate/project customer (from ~200 B2B accounts) requests payment plan for outstanding invoice(s); or AR aging shows customer 30+ days overdue; or customer proactively contacts BuildRight regarding cash flow difficulties
Frequency: ~15–25 payment plan negotiations/month (primarily during post-project billing phase for corporate accounts)
Volume: Affects ~200 corporate/institutional accounts with Net 60–90 day terms; ~10–15% may require payment restructuring at any time
Owner: Credit Manager
Participants: Credit Manager, Credit Analyst, AR Collector, Sales Manager (B2B), CFO, Customer (Finance/Procurement contact)
Source: workflow W1326 — Customer B2B Project Payment Plan Negotiation, Arrears Management &amp; Restructuring</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1326_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1326_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1326_Lane2" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1326_Lane3" name="Credit Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1326_Lane4" name="AR Collector">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1326_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1326_Start6" name="Corporate/project customer (from ~200 B2B accounts) requests payment plan for outstanding…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1326_Task7" name="Arrears identification &amp; escalation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Arrears identification &amp; escalation: System identifies overdue invoices per AR aging report: (a) 30 days overdue: system sends automated past-due reminder per W892; (b) 45 days overdue: AR Collector contacts customer for payment commitment; (c) 60 days overdue (past credit terms): Credit Analyst reviews account; if customer indicates inability to pay in full, escalates to Credit Manager for payment plan negotiation; (d) system flags account as &quot;Payment Plan Candidate&quot; with total outstanding, days overdue, customer payment history, and account lifetime value
Responsible (R): System / AR Collector / Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 1–2 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1326_Task8" name="Customer financial assessment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer financial assessment: Before negotiation, Credit Analyst assesses customer&#x27;s financial situation: (a) payment history: has customer paid on time previously? is this a one-time delay or recurring pattern? (b) outstanding exposure: total AR balance including current invoices not yet due; (c) customer credit score: current score per FIN-044 monitoring; (d) external signals: has customer&#x27;s business been affected by economic downturn, natural disaster, or project cancellation? (e) account value: annual revenue from customer, margin contribution, and strategic importance (government accounts, major developers); (f) Credit Analyst prepares recommendation: (i) standard payment plan (installments over 60–90 days), (ii) extended terms (restructure to longer payment period), (iii) accelerated collection (legal demand if high-risk), or (iv) write-off per W81 if uncollectable
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): Credit Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1326_Task9" name="Payment plan negotiation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Payment plan negotiation: Credit Manager contacts customer&#x27;s Finance/Procurement contact: (a) discuss reason for non-payment: cash flow timing, project dispute, billing error, or financial distress; (b) if project dispute: coordinate with Sales Manager and Category Manager to resolve dispute (material quality per W110, quantity discrepancy per W109) before payment plan discussion; (c) negotiate payment plan terms: (i) Standard installment plan: total outstanding split into 3–6 equal monthly payments; no interest if paid per schedule; (ii) Partial payment with extended terms: customer pays 30–50% immediately; remaining balance restructured over 90–180 days with 1% monthly late payment charge; (iii) Project milestone payment: payment aligned with customer&#x27;s own project billing milestones (common for government and developer accounts); customer provides copy of their project billing schedule as commitment; (d) Credit Manager documents negotiated terms in system; customer confirms in writing (email or signed payment plan agreement)
Responsible (R): Credit Manager / Customer
Accountable (A): CFO (plans &gt; PHP 2M)
Duration: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1326_Task10" name="Approval &amp; formalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Approval &amp; formalization: (a) Credit Manager submits payment plan for approval: (i) plans ≤ PHP 1M: Credit Manager approves; (ii) plans PHP 1M–5M: CFO approves; (iii) plans &gt; PHP 5M: CEO approves; (b) CFO reviews: (i) total exposure vs. customer lifetime value, (ii) risk of non-payment under the plan, (iii) impact on BuildRight&#x27;s cash flow, (iv) precedent risk (will other customers request similar terms?); (c) if approved: system creates formal Payment Plan record linked to original invoice(s); payment schedule auto-generated with due dates and amounts; (d) if not approved: Credit Manager re-negotiates with customer or escalates to accelerated collection per W1381; (e) system updates customer account with &quot;Active Payment Plan&quot; status; new orders may require COD or deposit per Credit Manager&#x27;s recommendation
Responsible (R): Credit Manager / CFO
Accountable (A): CEO (plans &gt; PHP 5M)
Duration: 1–2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1326_Task11" name="Payment plan monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment plan monitoring: AR Collector monitors payment plan compliance: (a) system generates payment reminders 5 days before each installment due date; (b) AR Collector follows up within 3 business days of missed installment; (c) if customer misses 2 consecutive installments: payment plan defaults — full outstanding balance immediately due; Credit Manager assesses next action: re-negotiate (one-time) or escalate to legal demand; (d) if customer pays per plan: system tracks compliance and removes &quot;Active Payment Plan&quot; flag upon completion; customer credit score improves per FIN-044 upon successful completion; (e) monthly: Credit Manager reviews all active payment plans — total exposure, compliance rate, aging of plans, and expected collection timeline
Responsible (R): AR Collector / Credit Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min/plan/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1326_Task12" name="Post-plan account normalization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Post-plan account normalization: Upon successful plan completion: (a) system restores customer to standard credit terms; (b) Credit Analyst reviews whether original credit limit and payment terms remain appropriate — may adjust per FIN-044; (c) if customer&#x27;s financial situation has deteriorated permanently: consider reducing credit limit, shortening payment terms, or converting to COD; (d) Sales Manager briefed on account status to manage customer relationship appropriately; (e) lessons learned feed into Credit Analyst&#x27;s assessment for future credit decisions per W886
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / Credit Manager / Sales Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 1 hour/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1326_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1326_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1326_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1326_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-288 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Payment &amp; Settlement (PA-16.3).) | - operational: formalizing plans as one-time arrangements and adjusting credit terms upon completion
Owner: Credit Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1326_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1326_Annotation14" targetRef="W1326_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
