    <bpmn:process id="W_W1327" name="W1327. Customer Trade Account Spend Analysis, Category Insights &amp; Quarterly Business Review" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Quarterly trade account review calendar; or triggered by significant account change (new project, payment issue, competitor win/loss)
Frequency: Quarterly business reviews for top 100 trade accounts; annual reviews for remaining ~5,100 trade accounts
Volume: 100 quarterly reviews (top accounts, 400/yr) + ~5,100 annual reviews = ~5,500 reviews per year
Owner: Sales Manager (B2B)
Participants: Sales Manager, Category Manager, Credit Analyst, Trade Account Customer (Procurement/Owner), Marketing Coordinator
Source: workflow W1327 — Customer Trade Account Spend Analysis, Category Insights &amp; Quarterly Business Review</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1327_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1327_Lane1" name="Credit Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1327_Lane2" name="Sales Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1327_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1327_Start4" name="Quarterly trade account review calendar; or triggered by significant account change (new…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1327_Task5" name="Spend data preparation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Spend data preparation: Credit Analyst compiles quarterly spend analysis for each top 100 trade account: (a) total spend: quarter vs. prior quarter vs. same quarter prior year; (b) category breakdown: spend per product category (lumber, plumbing, electrical, tiles, tools, etc.) with percentage share; (c) trend analysis: growing categories, declining categories, new categories purchased; (d) average order value and order frequency; (e) preferred fulfillment channels: in-store vs. BOPIS vs. delivery vs. special order (W38); (f) margin analysis: account&#x27;s gross margin contribution vs. trade account average; (g) competitive intelligence: Sales Manager notes any known competitor purchases by the account (from W624 competitor visits and Sales Associate field intelligence); (h) payment behavior: on-time payment rate, average days-to-pay, any payment plan history per W1326
Responsible (R): Credit Analyst / System
Accountable (A): Sales Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1327_Task6" name="Opportunity identification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Opportunity identification: Sales Manager and Category Manager jointly identify growth opportunities per account: (a) cross-sell: categories where the account under-purchases vs. their project profile (e.g., a contractor buying lumber but not tiles — are they sourcing tiles elsewhere?); (b) up-sell: higher-margin alternatives or premium brands in categories where the account currently buys economy; (c) new service adoption: has the account tried installation referral per W904, BOM estimation per W820, tool rental per W139, project delivery per W980?; (d) volume incentive: is the account approaching a rebate tier per W27 that would reward increased spend?; (e) project pipeline: any known upcoming projects that BuildRight can pre-quote per W58?
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / Category Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 1–2 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1327_Task7" name="Quarterly Business Review (QBR) meeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Quarterly Business Review (QBR) meeting: Sales Manager conducts QBR with customer (in-person at customer&#x27;s office or BuildRight Pro Desk, or video call for remote accounts): (a) present spend analysis: highlight the account&#x27;s purchasing trends and how BuildRight has supported their projects; (b) discuss upcoming projects and material requirements: customer shares project pipeline; BuildRight commits to pricing and availability; (c) present growth opportunities: cross-sell categories, volume incentive tiers, new services; (d) solicit feedback: (i) what is BuildRight doing well? (ii) what can be improved? (iii) are there stock-out issues in specific categories? (iv) how does BuildRight compare to competitors on price, availability, and service? (e) resolve any open issues: credit terms, delivery problems, quality concerns, returns pending; (f) agree on action items with owners and deadlines
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / Customer
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 45–60 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1327_Task8" name="Competitive retention action">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Competitive retention action: If spend analysis reveals declining purchases or competitive intelligence indicates customer buying from competitors: (a) Sales Manager develops retention proposal: (i) matched pricing on competitive categories per W329, (ii) extended credit terms per W1326, (iii) priority delivery scheduling per W980, (iv) dedicated account coordinator; (b) VP Merchandising approves any pricing exceptions; (c) Sales Manager presents retention offer to customer; (d) system tracks retention actions and outcomes
Responsible (R): Sales Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1327_Task9" name="Post-QBR action tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Post-QBR action tracking: Sales Manager logs all QBR outcomes and action items in CRM: (a) customer feedback themes aggregated per W87; (b) stock-out or availability issues escalated to Category Manager for supply planning review per W31; (c) cross-sell/up-sell commitments tracked to conversion; (d) competitive pricing intelligence shared with Category Manager per W130; (e) action items tracked to completion with weekly Sales Manager follow-up; (f) results feed into next quarter&#x27;s QBR preparation
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / System
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 30 min/account</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1327_Task10" name="Annual account stratification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Annual account stratification: Annually, Sales Manager and Credit Analyst stratify all 5,200 trade accounts: (a) Platinum (top 50 accounts, &gt; PHP 5M/year): dedicated account manager, quarterly QBR, priority service, custom pricing; (b) Gold (next 200 accounts, PHP 1–5M/year): semi-annual business review, preferential terms, proactive engagement; (c) Silver (next 1,000 accounts, PHP 200K–1M/year): annual review, standard trade terms; (d) Bronze (remaining ~4,000 accounts, &lt; PHP 200K/year): self-service with annual statement review; (e) stratification drives resource allocation: Sales Manager time, Category Manager engagement, and credit terms per tier
Responsible (R): Sales Manager / Credit Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–5 days (annual)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1327_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1327_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1327_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1327_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-288 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Payment &amp; Settlement (PA-16.3).) | - operational: preparing tangible insights (spend analysis, savings opportunities) that demonstrate QBR value; operational: customer master data governance per W292 and loyalty account linkage; operational: VP Merchandising oversight and quarterly review of pricing exception frequency
Owner: Sales Manager (B2B)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1327_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1327_Annotation12" targetRef="W1327_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow14" sourceRef="W1327_Start4" targetRef="W1327_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow15" sourceRef="W1327_Task5" targetRef="W1327_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow16" sourceRef="W1327_Task6" targetRef="W1327_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow17" sourceRef="W1327_Task7" targetRef="W1327_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow18" sourceRef="W1327_Task8" targetRef="W1327_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow19" sourceRef="W1327_Task9" targetRef="W1327_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1327_Flow20" sourceRef="W1327_Task10" targetRef="W1327_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1327_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1327_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1327">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task5_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task5"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1450" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1327_Start4_di" bpmnElement="W1327_Start4"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
