    <bpmn:process id="W_W1381" name="W1381. Customer Bounced Check (DAIF) Resolution, Legal Action &amp; BIR Reporting" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Bank notifies BuildRight that a deposited customer check was returned unpaid (DAIF — &quot;Drawn Against Insufficient Funds&quot; or account closed)
Frequency: ~15–25 bounced checks/month across all entities
Volume: ~200–300 bounced checks/year; average bounced check value PHP 50,000–300,000
Owner: AR Supervisor
Participants: AR Clerk, AR Supervisor, Legal, Finance Manager, Customer, Bank
Source: workflow W1381 — Customer Bounced Check (DAIF) Resolution, Legal Action &amp; BIR Reporting</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1381_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1381_Lane1" name="Bank">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1381_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1381_Lane3" name="AR Clerk">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1381_Lane4" name="Legal">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1381_Lane5" name="AR Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_Task16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1381_End17</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1381_Start7" name="Bank notifies BuildRight that a deposited customer check was returned unpaid (DAIF —…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task8" name="Bank notifies AR Clerk of returned check; AR Clerk receives bank return memo…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bank notifies AR Clerk of returned check; AR Clerk receives bank return memo with reason code (DAIF — insufficient funds, DAUD — uncleared deposits, account closed, stop payment, etc.)
Responsible (R): Bank / AR Clerk
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1381_Task9" name="System reverses the PDC deposit in two entries: (a) reverse deposit: Dr. PDC…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: System reverses the PDC deposit in two entries: (a) reverse deposit: Dr. PDC Receivable / Cr. Cash in Bank; (b) reinstate receivable: Dr. Accounts Receivable — Customer / Cr. PDC Receivable; the AR invoice is reactivated in aging with status &quot;Overdue — Bounced Check&quot;; PDC register status updated to &quot;Bounced — DAIF/DAUD&quot; (financial reversal executed with W425)
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task10" name="AR Clerk contacts customer within 24 hours: (a) notifies customer of bounced…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AR Clerk contacts customer within 24 hours: (a) notifies customer of bounced check, (b) requests immediate replacement payment (cash, manager&#x27;s check, or online transfer), (c) warns of BP 22 legal consequences if not resolved within 5 banking days, (d) posts the Returned Check Fee debit memo — standard penalty plus bank charges (PHP 500–2,000 per returned check): Dr. Accounts Receivable / Cr. Other Income (penalty posting executed with W425)
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 15 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task11" name="If customer provides replacement payment within 5 banking days: process payment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: If customer provides replacement payment within 5 banking days: process payment per standard W8; update PDC register status to &quot;Replaced — Resolved&quot;; no further action
Responsible (R): AR Clerk
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 5 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task12" name="If customer does not resolve within 5 banking days: AR Supervisor escalates to…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: If customer does not resolve within 5 banking days: AR Supervisor escalates to Legal; Legal prepares and sends formal demand letter via registered mail with return card (required per BP 22 before filing criminal complaint); demand letter gives customer 5 banking days from receipt to make good the check
Responsible (R): Legal
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 1 hour/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task13" name="If customer still does not pay after demand letter: (a) Legal evaluates whether…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: If customer still does not pay after demand letter: (a) Legal evaluates whether to file BP 22 criminal complaint with prosecutor&#x27;s office — decision based on amount (generally filed for &gt; PHP 50,000), customer relationship value, and likelihood of recovery; (b) for amounts &lt; PHP 50,000 or strategic customers: Finance Manager may approve extended payment plan or settlement negotiation instead of legal action; (c) system flags account for credit hold — no new credit sales per W572
Responsible (R): Legal / Finance Manager
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: 30 min/case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task14" name="If BP 22 complaint filed: Legal manages prosecution process (affidavit…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: If BP 22 complaint filed: Legal manages prosecution process (affidavit, evidence submission, court hearings); timeline: 6–18 months to resolution in Philippine courts
Responsible (R): Legal
Accountable (A): CFO
Duration: As needed</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task15" name="Monthly: AR Supervisor prepares DAIF summary report — bounced check count…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly: AR Supervisor prepares DAIF summary report — bounced check count, total value, resolution rate (replaced, settled, legal), average days to resolution; Finance Manager reviews and adjusts credit terms for repeat offenders
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Finance Manager
Duration: 1 hour/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow28</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1381_Task16" name="Annual: AR Supervisor compiles DAIF listing for BIR reporting — all bounced…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 9: Annual: AR Supervisor compiles DAIF listing for BIR reporting — all bounced checks received during the year with customer TIN, check details, and resolution status; included in Annual Information Return (AIF) per BIR requirements
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: 4 hours/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow28</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1381_Flow29</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1381_End17" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1381_Flow29</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1381_Annotation18">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-288 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Payment &amp; Settlement (PA-16.3).) | - operational: AR Supervisor review and approval gate
Owner: AR Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
