      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1524" name="W1524. Philippine Government &amp; Institutional Customer Tax-Exempt Sales Processing, BIR-Compliant Documentation &amp; OR Requirements" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Government agency, LGU, state university, or tax-exempt institution presents purchase order with tax exemption certificate
Frequency: ~200–400 tax-exempt transactions/month across 200 stores (~1–2 per store per month)
Volume: Average transaction value: PHP 10,000–500,000 (government procurement of construction materials for public infrastructure, school buildings, barangay halls)
Owner: AR Supervisor
Participants: AR Supervisor, Cashier/Sales Rep, Store Manager, Customer (government purchasing officer), Tax Compliance Manager
Source: workflow W1524 — Philippine Government &amp; Institutional Customer Tax-Exempt Sales Processing, BIR-Compliant Documentation &amp; OR Requirements</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1524_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1524_Lane1" name="Cashier">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1524_Lane2" name="Delivery Staff">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1524_Lane3" name="AR Supervisor">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1524_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1524_Start5" name="Government agency, LGU, state university, or tax-exempt institution presents purchase…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1524_Task6" name="Tax exemption verification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Tax exemption verification: (a) customer presents government purchase order (PO) or purchase request with: (i) agency/LGU letterhead, (ii) authorized signatory, (iii) fund allocation reference (allotment class), (iv) tax exemption certificate or BIR ruling; (b) Cashier/Sales Rep verifies: (i) tax exemption document is current (not expired — most have annual renewal), (ii) purchasing officer has authorization letter from agency head, (iii) agency is on BIR&#x27;s list of VAT-exempt entities; (c) if verification passes: proceed with tax-exempt sale; if uncertain: escalate to AR Supervisor; if clearly ineligible: inform customer that standard VAT applies
Responsible (R): Cashier / Sales Rep
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1524_Task7" name="Transaction processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Transaction processing: (a) Cashier creates sales order/transaction in POS with: (i) customer account linked to government entity master (separate from retail customer), (ii) VAT treatment set to &quot;Exempt&quot; (not zero-rated — these have different BIR treatments), (iii) PO number and fund allocation reference recorded; (b) system calculates: (i) item prices net of VAT (standard prices are VAT-inclusive per BuildRight&#x27;s pricing policy — system backs out 12% VAT), (ii) total amount exempt; (c) Store Manager authorizes tax-exempt transaction (requires manager override in POS to prevent unauthorized VAT removal)
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1524_Task8" name="BIR-compliant documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: BIR-compliant documentation: (a) system generates: (i) Sales Invoice (SI) with: &quot;VAT EXEMPT&quot; printed prominently, customer TIN, agency name and address, PO reference, item details with unit prices (net of VAT), total amount, &quot;VAT Exempt pursuant to Section 109 of the NIRC&quot; notation; (ii) Official Receipt (OR) with matching details; (b) Cashier attaches: (i) copy of tax exemption certificate, (ii) copy of purchase order, (iii) copy of authorized purchasing officer ID; (c) all documents stapled/filed in store&#x27;s government transaction folder for BIR audit readiness
Responsible (R): Cashier / System
Accountable (A): AR Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1524_Task9" name="Delivery and acceptance">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Delivery and acceptance: (a) if order includes delivery: Delivery Receipt (DR) generated with matching SI number; (b) government customer&#x27;s receiving officer signs DR with date and official stamp; (c) signed DR returned to store and filed with SI/OR documentation package
Responsible (R): Delivery Staff / Customer
Accountable (A): Store Manager
Duration: Delivery per schedule</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1524_Task10" name="Payment collection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Payment collection: (a) government customer payment typically via: (i) government check (MDS check from DBM or local treasury check), (ii) bank transfer to BuildRight&#x27;s bank account; (b) AR Supervisor verifies: (i) check details match SI amount exactly (government cannot pay more or less than invoiced amount), (ii) check is from the correct government fund (some agencies have multiple accounts); (c) AR Supervisor applies payment to customer account with government check reference number; (d) if payment via MDS check: deposit to BuildRight&#x27;s bank — government checks clear within 1–3 banking days
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 15–20 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1524_Task11" name="Monthly reconciliation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Monthly reconciliation: (a) AR Supervisor compiles all government tax-exempt sales for the month: (i) total exempt sales amount, (ii) list of government entities, (iii) corresponding SI/OR numbers; (b) Tax Compliance Manager reviews for BIR VAT return preparation: exempt sales must be correctly reported in the monthly/quarterly VAT return (BIR Form 2550Q/2550M) in the &quot;exempt sales&quot; column; (c) documentation package archived for 10-year BIR audit retention per A6.5
Responsible (R): AR Supervisor / Tax Compliance Manager
Accountable (A): Finance Controller
Duration: 2–3 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1524_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1524_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1524_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1524_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-288 (ensure controlled execution — Customer Payment &amp; Settlement (PA-16.3).) | - operational: AR Supervisor review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: AR Supervisor</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1524_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1524_Annotation13" targetRef="W1524_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow15" sourceRef="W1524_Start5" targetRef="W1524_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow16" sourceRef="W1524_Task6" targetRef="W1524_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow17" sourceRef="W1524_Task7" targetRef="W1524_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow18" sourceRef="W1524_Task8" targetRef="W1524_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow19" sourceRef="W1524_Task9" targetRef="W1524_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow20" sourceRef="W1524_Task10" targetRef="W1524_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1524_Flow21" sourceRef="W1524_Task11" targetRef="W1524_End12" />
    </bpmn:process>
